; The layout keeps no undo history, so no key takes back the echo
; area's placement.
> (buffers:silent? layout:buffer)
#t
; The echo area sits at the bottom of the screen at depth 90, outside the
; level of the user's windows; parts placed at the bottom are ordered by
; depth, then in the order placed.
> (tree)
(layout:level () (layout-split:container ((direction . column)) (layout:level () #(views:view ((view . 1) (buffer . "*scratch*")))) #(views:view ((view . 3) (buffer . " *Echo Area*") (depth . 90) (size . content) (locked . #t)))))
