(options:set! "-1 is not a valid value for echo-area:log-max")
; A killed log made again by another module's code keeps no undo after
; that module unloads, and one made again by code acting for no module,
; such as advice on batch-ended, is made all the same.
> (buffers:kill! (buffers:find "*Messages*"))
#t
